Dimension Tables table

•	Dimension Table contains detailed information of the fact and it has primary keys 
•	Dimension table will not contain duplicates 
•	Dimension tables are the parent table of fact tables 
•	Fact tables will join with Dimension tables.
•	Dimension tables will have master data, so while loading the data, we have to load the dimension table first, and fact table next. 
•	While doing the data clean-up, we have to remove the fact table data first and then we have to remove the dimension table data, 
since fact and dimension tables are having the integrity constraint relationship between them
•	We follow SCD type 2 in our project
   SCD Type 2 (Slowly Changing Dimension Type 2) is a data warehouse technique used to maintain historical
   records when a dimension attribute changes, instead of overwriting the old value.
  ex:  
   Suppose a bank customer, Priya, lives in Chennai in January. In June, she moves to Bengaluru.
  If we simply update her city in the data warehouse, the old value Chennai is lost.
  SCD Type 2 preserves both the old and new versions.

•	Dimension tables are having the master data, so that we have to load the dimension first
  and we will have the types like Slowly change dimensions and late arriving dimensions


